Greetings oh wise and noble netters, and oh-so benificent of
development teams.

I would like to congratulate you on an *INCREDIBLE* job of porting
Nethack to the macintosh.  I have had no bug problems with the game,
and the implementation of the dialogue boxes et al is marvelous.

I do have a couple of suggestions and problems...

Is it necessary to have Nethack return to the finder after each game?
I think that a 'would you like to play again' line would be most time
saving for us beginning net-hackers who die a lot on the first few
levels, and wish to restart immediately.  I fixed this on nethack
2.something by turning nethack into a finder, but since I purchased a
hard drive , that is no longer an option...

Is it also necessary to put the bones files in the system folder?  I
find that that folder is quite cluttered with just my inits, cdevs,
printing resources, and all... Could they perhaps go in the Nethack
folder? Even, wonder of wonders, a new folder inside the nethack
folder that holds all of the game files?

By the way, is there any way to change the wizardname default from h+
without recompiling?

Oh, by the way, for the gentleman who is having problems double
clicking on the save file... you may have one of two (or more)
problems
1. Your bundle bits are screwed up. I had this problem when I unpacked
nethack also. I couldn't even see the nifty new Icon for it... I would
suggest setting the bundle bit on Nethack using Disktop, DeskZap, or
some other file utility... BundAid is the easiest to use, and it is
available from the info-mac archives at sumex-aim...
2. You could be using a Init such as DesktopManager which splits your
desktop into little pieces. Sometimes owned files are lost with this
program. Drag it out of your system folder, and, although updating
your desktop will take longer, you will be able to double click till
your heart's content.
3. As another gentleperson said, rebuild your desktop.


Thanks all for your help, and your valuable time reading silly
messages.

